  "setup": "Mac Studio M2 Max, QEMU/HVF Linux VM Space (2 vCPU, 2 GiB), same host, through the cua daemon, with the bulk lane (the VM's second disk, `bulk.img`) carrying files of 2 MiB and more; this branch's cua-spacesd overlaid and the image's udev rule applied. Measured 2026-10-20 (run 2 of two; exec p50 varied 0.79-1.24 ms between runs, hence the 1.5x allowance). Without the lane, the same build does 360 MiB/s up and 241 MiB/s down for 100 MiB (CUA_BULK_LANE=off); the user-mode network is the ceiling (raw slirp TCP 257-371 MiB/s). p95 is kept only for the metrics with 20 or more samples.",
